              '<li><strong>Role of Education & Civic Symbols:</strong> Public schools, national festivals, and shared constitutional ideals continually renew Renan\'s "daily plebiscite" across new generations without suppressing regional cultural pride.</li>' +
              '<li><strong>Self-Determination vs. Territorial Integrity:</strong> While anti-colonial nationalism invoked self-determination to end foreign rule, modern international law balances self-determination with protecting minority rights inside democratic, federal states.</li>' +
              '<li><strong>Economic & Infrastructural Integration:</strong> Railways, postal networks, and a unified national market under India\'s constitutional framework connect distant states, turning abstract brotherhood into everyday interdependence.</li>' +
              '</ul>'
